WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.520
And so, let's all have a listen.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.270
Dear Hell...

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.570
Jigoku mitai ni asobitai
I want to have a good time like Hell

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.700
Jigoku mitai ni yasumitai
I want to rest like Hell

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.540
Jigoku mitai na nidoneshite
I want to go back to sleep like Hell

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.130
Teiji de agaritai
And finish work on time

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.970
Jigoku mitai ni tabesugite
I ate too much like Hell

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.720
Jigoku mitai ni nomisugita
I drank too much like Hell

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.980
Aa sonna wake de
Ah, for these reasons

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.230
Jigoku mitai
It's like Hell

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.650
Sonna toki koso deban desu
At such a time it's all the more his turn on stage

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.320
Hoozuki-sama ga moriageru
Mr. Hozuki livens things up

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.410
Omakase kudasai!
Please leave it to me!

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:03.000
Aa jigoku jigoku mainichi jigoku
Ah, Hell, Hell, every day Hell

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.580
Jigoku jigoku
Hell, Hell

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.250
"Uso desho?!"
"You can't mean that, right?!"

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.170
Jigoku jigoku youkoso jigoku
Hell, Hell, welcome to Hell

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.010
Atchi muite
Look that way

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.590
Kotchi muite
Look this way

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.720
Abikyoukan!
Pandemonium!

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.090
Gongo! Doudan!
What the hell!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.890
Shitsureishimashita!
Pardon me!

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:23.890
Sonna kanji no
In that kind of way

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.980
A! Jigoku desu! Jajajajan!
Ah! It's Hell! Ta ta ta-da!

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.980
Katsu!
Curses!

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.820
REST AREA
TEA

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:44.910
Momotaro threw aside the glory of his past
and looked toward the future.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.830
The Inch-High Samurai
stopped thinking of himself as unfortunate.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.640
Deep down I've been thinking I also need
to get over some things... recently...

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.220
Fundamentally

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:13.730
Leaving aside whether you've actually conquered it,
I think you're certainly channeling it well.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:19.950
Which is why I want you to be confident
just the way you are and continue to race ahead...

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.580
I'm gonna get swayed by the encouragement
this guy's offering me...

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.870
No, you're wrong. No matter the place...

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:36.340
when I hear "tanu... tanuki," I totally lose it, and lash out
with the poor precision of a common foot soldier.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.760
I must control my aim and attack only the dead.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.100
I want to become Go*go 13.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.020
Mustard, even if you do lash out indiscriminately
like a common foot solider,

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.650
your weapon is something like a Gatling gun,
so I don't see any problem...

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.610
No! If my trauma's something that can be overcome,
then I'd definitely like to do so!

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.120
I want to train my mind and become even stronger!

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.540
I see...

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:13.130
However, when I remember that guy,
I end up flying into a rage.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:19.300
I get it: Not everything about the way I react is bad.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.800
But, I still want to do something about it.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:27.930
Which is why I'd like to ask you, someone who's
always capable of restraining me if I get out of hand,

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.020
to stick with me through this.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.900
Sorry to ask, considering you're so busy, but I beg you.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:39.070
Well, I don't mind doing it,
but just how should we approach this...?

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.490
Training... Training, huh?

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.580
Ah, this talk of training
just reminded me of a certain place.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.420
There's actually a temple down in Hell?

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.340
There is, indeed. Although it seems
not many people come here.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.170
KONPON-JI TEMPLE

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:03.220
KONPON-JI
TEMPLE

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.670
Funerals... aren't exactly a thing here, after all.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.340
Temples are not primarily places
for holding funerals, you know.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.010
They're places where monks train,
so they're naturally ideal for training.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.060
Makes sense!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.310
I'll do my best!

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.900
I'm Shukaku, the head priest of Konpon-ji Temple.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.530
I'm Hakuzosu, and I'm likewise the head priest here.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.370
YOU DAMNED TANUKI!

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:27.620
Hi-yah!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.370
Impressive!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.500
What a rabbit you are...

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.710
You're one to get hotheaded all of a sudden, I see.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.630
Beyond that, you're overly optimistic!

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.380
See? Whether in terms of your honor or strength,
this place will help train you, right?

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.350
Wh-what's going on here?

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.730
Ah, sorry about that, Bunbuku.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.560
Bunbuku's a tanuki?!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:58.650
That's right. Long ago in the Mundane World
at a place called Morin-ji Temple,

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.070
there was a senior priest named Shukaku
who had a mysterious teakettle...

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.820
The Shukaku you speak of is none other than myself.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.410
Well, come on in. Take a seat.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.490
Very well.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:20.040
My true form is that of a tanuki, but I've served tea
that brings good fortune to people,

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.420
and I've performed various feats in front of them, too.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:27.640
"Always bring smiles to
the faces of others." That is my creed.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:32.220
And this little guy here is the true form of the
tea kettle that pours good-fortune-bringing tea:

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.060
Bunbuku Chagama.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.890
I'm High Priest Shukaku's apprentice.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.770
Have some tea.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.480
So, as for the feats I performed...

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:42.860
Master! Master!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:48.320
Let's hold off on any further self-introductions
for now and first hear what brings these two here.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.030
Ah, my apologies. Wasn't intentional.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.250
Master loves sharing stories of his past, you see.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.790
Also, he's essentially an old man,
so on top of his stories being long,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:01.960
he repeats the same things again and again.
Just keep that in mind.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:08.010
Bunbuku Chagama, I sense the same kind of pessimism
coming from you that I see from Momotaro nowadays.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:13.600
UDON
RICE
SOBA

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.390
Anyway, isn't it kind of odd
that you have two head priests here?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.930
They really are both head priests.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:21.560
This temple was opened as a gathering place to
deepen understanding between tanuki and foxes,

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.150
who have vied with each other for many years...

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.240
But neither of them will give up
their position as head priest,

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:30.240
so for the time being, they both serve in that role.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.410
I see. What an uneasy situation.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.660
By the way, I, Hakuzosu, am a virtuous female fox

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.040
who served at a temple
in the Mundane World for many years.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:42.540
Pleased to meet you.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.630
She bit a monk to death and is now
impersonating him, so be careful!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:47.800
What brings ya here?!

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:53.600
The rabbit from Crackling Mountain has come here
to overcome her trauma surrounding tanuki.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.810
Watch it!

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.310
I-I see...
Kill me! I'd rather be killed!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:06:59.690
Kill me! I'd rather be killed!

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:04.190
Looks like she could pop
a blood vessel any moment. She alright?
Kill me! I'd rather be killed!

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:06.610
KONPON-JI TEMPLE

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.780
Well then, first we'll start with seated Zen meditation.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.700
Don't lose your composure. Look only at yourself.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.870
Your place within this world...

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.420
Your place within the universe...

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:30.800
How small your trauma is
in the grand scheme of the great big world...

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.850
Ooh!

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.930
To think you managed to defend against my Zen stick...

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.350
Impressive!

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.310
You were standing behind me, so I just kinda...

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:45.400
Seems someone has mastered
the ways of Go*go before me!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.900
I'd like to try that, too.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.780
Is it alright if I position myself
even further back, behind you?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.410
This isn't something you do out of curiosity!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.040
In any case, I did feel serene for a moment there.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:58.790
A break! Let's take a break! Tea! It's time for tea!

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:00.120
Ah, the tanuki!
A break! Let's take a break! Tea! It's time for tea!

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:00.960
A break! Let's take a break! Tea! It's time for tea!

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.790
Oh! You're still traumatized,
but it does seem there's been some progress.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.840
Good grief...

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:17.970
Now that I've gotten more gray around the fur,
my strikes with the Zen stick have lost their punch.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.180
In bygone days...

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.810
Master, it's been so long since we've had visitors

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.940
that I suppose you can't help but want
to talk about yourself, huh?

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:30.610
I-i-it's just fine. Please share some stories.
This is another aspect of my training.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.200
Oh! Very well, listen to this.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:39.080
Long ago, I showed people skillful feats
such as tightrope walking and magic tricks.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:43.750
You did some shapeshifting, too.
You used to have sharper skills back in the day.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.630
That's right. I used to be able to stretch out
to eight tatami mats in size,

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.840
but nowadays four and a half mats
is the very best I can do.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:58.100
Don't exaggerate! You can't do any more
than three mats at best now, right?

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.810
Cut it out with the bland, dirty jokes about tanuki.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.190
Ah, it's just like Master to make tanuki jokes
of that sort. Simply ignore them, please.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.730
Bunbuku Chagama, I've begun to get the sense
that I should ask you to teach her instead.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:15.320
Oh, that's right. I've instructed Bunbuku
on how to pull off every single one of my tricks.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.200
Since we're taking a break anyway,
how about I have him show them to you?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:25.710
Oh, that sounds good. If she can enjoy watching a
tanuki perform some tricks, she's made further progress.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.920
Th-that's true...

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:29.290
Hup!

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.130
They say that "art brings bread."

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.760
Not only does this entertain people,

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.260
it's effective training for interviews
that make unreasonable requests of you.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.270
I honestly don't want to work for a company
that requires an interview like that.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.940
When you put smiles on people's faces,
it makes you happy as well.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.320
There's nothing more fun than that!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.320
Miss Rabbit, this here is the true essence of a tanuki.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.910
We are big-hearted animals that make people laugh.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:04.540
We're not seen as being malicious like foxes!
We're animals of a soothing sort!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:08.370
It's simply uncalled for to say
you're not malicious like foxes are!

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.840
Tanuki just don't know when to shut up.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.630
You're an apprentice, right?! You better watch it!

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.590
But isn't it the truth?!

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:20.640
Miss Rabbit, foxes are naturally
better animals, you know.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.390
They're divine messengers and very clever to boot.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.810
There's no need to force yourself to like tanuki.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:33.150
Shut your mouth, Fox. After all, Miss Rabbit,
you came here today to hear what tanuki have to say.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:38.780
Didn't she come here to train?! If what I have to say
is useful, she should listen to both of us.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:43.700
Foxes sure are unpleasant...
They're on edge about everything, right, Miss Rabbit?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:49.210
Isn't the way tanuki try to sweet-talk you
about everything even more troubling, Miss Rabbit?

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:52.460
Miss Rabbit, Miss Rabbit, what do you think?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.420
Why not use this opportunity to try becoming a tanuki?

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.880
No, it's the foxes who're clever.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.470
Tanuki are great too, you know!

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:13.610
Earlier, you said this temple was opened as a place
tanuki and foxes could come together, did you not?

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.160
I somehow feel a lot better now. Sorry.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:28.870
Fundamentally, the way you're programmed to see us
as enemies simply won't go away, will it?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.970
GRASS

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:54.060
I wonder just how strong I am these days.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:55.690
"Strong"?

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:00.570
Am I able to measure up to all
the other Hell minion animals?

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:04.740
Oh... There are many carnivores
among the other animals, so...

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.620
I wonder how you'd fare.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.240
Chocolate Vine Tea

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.330
Shall we ask them to participate in a tournament?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.250
Mixed Martial Arts Contest

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.800
Rat versus rabbit.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.760
Hi-yah!

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.100
SQUEEEEEEAAAAAK!

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:29.810
Next.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.060
Dog versus rabbit.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.150
Hi-yah!

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.240
SNAKE
RABBIT

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.900
Snake versus rabbit.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.660
WOLF
RABBIT

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.330
Wolf versus rabbit.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.750
I-I give up.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:59.300
Right now, there's a revolution underway
between predators and prey.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:05.800
Thought you'd be tougher than that!
Come and face me again once you get stronger!

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:12.020
Sounds like something a boss would declare
to the hero in the opening stages of a role-playing game.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:16.190
It does seem this is a valuable way
to test your actual combat ability.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:17.900
Squeak.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:24.030
I think I'll use you to help get the public to more fully
acknowledge the world of Hell minion animals.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.200
This is a golden opportunity.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.250
A Cornered Rodent Will Bite a Cat
Decisive Bout

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.250
Watch for Free!!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.120
What's this?! Seems pretty interesting.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.500
I love the raw energy of these type of events, you know?

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:42.500
Come on by! Take a look!

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.010
June 9th Showdown
June 9th Showdown

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.130
Please do!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.470
A Cornered Rodent
Will Bite a Bear

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.550
Outsiders are also welcome to watch the fight!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.140
Feel free to take photos and upload video footage!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.970
I'm gonna go watch!

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:57.060
Does seem pretty interesting...

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.480
Alright, things are finally underway.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:06.200
ANALYST
BLOW-BY-BLOW
ANNOUNCER

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.070
It's the most dangerous dare in all of Hell.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:10.870
Miss Rabbit will challenge
a number of fierce beasts in battle!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:14.910
A rabbit she may be,
but she's a Hell minion nonetheless...

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.710
Although an extreme lightweight, she's still
the nuclear warhead of the Realm of Mincemeat!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.340
The Japanese hare... Mustard!

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:27.130
Oh, boy, I see there are even Hell minion rabbits, huh?
Blow-by-Blow Announcer Hozuki?

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.470
That's right, Analyst Rurio.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.140
Here in Hell, we are always recruiting
more Hell minion animals.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:38.190
All the feral dogs out there, all the bears, how about it?

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:42.560
Ah, you there on the TV studio staff,
is the onscreen text showing?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.320
Please make sure we broadcast it, okay?

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.950
King Shko (Specialist)
Out of consideration for the safety of the animals, the fights will be
held under the guidance of a specialist so as not to end in an animal
being torn limb from limb.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.780
That kind of thing's important nowadays.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:51.530
He's up to something again...

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.910
Well then, the first fierce beast
is already the favorite to win.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:15:00.170
A flame lion from Great Screaming Hell's
Realm of Fiery Lion Mauling...

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:02.330
Benihikari!

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.590
Sounds like a brand name for rice, doesn't it?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:15.100
The Realm of Fiery Lion Mauling is where those who
disrupt community harmony and cause trouble end up.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:19.060
As you can see, the realm
has flame lions that spew fire.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.810
But it's gotta be hot for you too, right?

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.730
Looks like you messed up
while jumping through a ring of fire.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:28.320
Your understanding of lions is pretty awful, you know...

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:36.790
Great Screaming Hell
Realm of
Fiery Lion Mauling
Red Hot River Realm

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:33.320
Great Screaming Hell has many lions.
There are lions in the Red Hot River Realm, as well.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.740
All you lions out there, please consider working here!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:41.080
Here in Hell, we are always recruiting
more Hell minion animals.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.040
I don't like how he keeps repeating that
like some kind of subliminal messaging.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.000
He's a black hole for personnel.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.380
Well then, the first one to land a decisive blow wins!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.720
The rabbit is leveraging her maneuverability
for some nifty footwork!

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:02.980
Whoa there! The lion's claws are lashing out
with ferociously robust speed!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:10.650
However, does Mustard, who's using the terrain
to toy with Benihikari, already have the edge?!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.280
Note: A major sea battle in the Genpei War.
It's just like the "leaping of eight ships"
from the Battle of Dan-no-ura!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:21.750
The rabbit can maintain full speed
while leaping and zigzagging around, after all.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:26.750
Not to mention it'd be a Herculean task to catch up
to Miss Mustard given all the training she does.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:31.050
What's with that pheasant's condescending attitude?

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.510
She did it!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.060
I'm beaten.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.640
Mustard has come out on top!

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.310
Once Benihikari tired out,
she downed him with a single blow!

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.980
This is the moment the rabbit got the better of the lion!

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:57.870
ANALYST
BLOW-BY-BLOW
ANNOUNCER

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:52.530
She managed to do it, that Mustard.
Her expression says she didn't even have to go all out.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:55.780
Although, she's never had much
of a facial expression to speak of.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.030
Next up...

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:03.290
The White Bulldozer of the Eight Cold Hells...
polar bear Polaris!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.960
Come on, Bear, get her good!

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:08.170
Hup!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.550
That was quick!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:19.470
Seems the heat of the Eight Greater Hells was hard
on an animal from the Eight Cold Hells, after all.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.430
Bear, wasn't that a bit pathetic?

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.940
Next, we have a gigantic elephant
from the Raining Fire Realm named Hanako!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:34.190
Here in Hell, we are also
recruiting Hell minion elephants.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:37.910
She's the boss of the Gigantic Elephant Group.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.120
DIRECTOR
DEPARTMENT HEADS
SECTION MANAGERS
EMPLOYEES
THE CHEERFUL HELL ELEPHANT GROUP

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:42.160
ANALYST
BLOW-BY-BLOW
ANNOUNCER

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:41.290
So with elephants, it's a female who's the boss, huh?

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.080
Yes.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:47.330
Despite being an herbivore, the elephant
is the king of land animals, feared even by lions.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:50.500
So now, just what will become of Mustard?

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.550
Oh boy, what's this?!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.970
She's running in circles and toying with her opponent!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:02.060
Somehow or other, there appears to be
loads of Mustards!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.310
It's the Clone Technique!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.310
It's enough to make even the elephant dizzy!

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:11.360
Note: Such a fate happened to a Tiger in the Children's book
"The Story of Little Black Sambo."

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:11.360
Miss Mustard's moving with such force,
she's liable to turn her into white butter!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.860
Note: Such a fate happened to a Tiger in the Children's book
"The Story of Little Black Sambo."
You're thinking of a tiger.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.070
The elephant has been defeated!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.280
Mustard's power is the real deal!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.990
Is the Japanese hare invincible?!

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:23.450
That brings to mind the invincible Spanish Armada.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:26.620
That Rurio's got an odd knack for analysis...

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.000
ANALYST
BLOW-BY-BLOW

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.000
ANNOUNCER

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.170
Well then, next is...

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.670
The vajra-beaked bird...

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:35.380
an airborne missile that never misses its target... Hayate!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:42.850
So, did he think up each of those catchphrases
on his own? The Chief of Staff, I mean.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:47.770
For whatever reason, he seems like the kinda guy
who never misses watching pro wrestling, you know?

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.440
HAAAA!

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.270
Ah-ha!

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.320
Just as you'd expected, she's a tactician,
that rabbit from Crackling Mountain!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:57.860
She anticipated an air battle
and had her boomerang ready!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.120
Mustard, on top of being painstakingly prepared,

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:07.290
is good at adjusting her strategy
to the circumstances, you see.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:12.000
Well, I think we can say simple physical attacks
won't be enough to beat her.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:16.380
Moreover, here in Hell, we are always recruiting
more Hell minion animals.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.220
He's like a broken record, this guy.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:24.720
Well, both the elephant and bird
were solidly defeated, huh, Hozuki?

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.100
They were, indeed.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:30.230
Considering how intensely Mustard trains,
I suppose that's no surprise, though...

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.650
Okay, it's finally time for today's main event!

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:39.950
Hell's armored fighting vehicle now stands
in the way of the nuclear warhead!

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:44.120
A single stroke of her claws takes a mere 0.01 seconds!

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:49.580
An extreme heavyweight,
they call her the Crimson Monster!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.830
Meow-ha-ha-ha.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.500
Lady Kasha!

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.380
"God damn!"

00:19:56.500 --> 00:20:00.130
God Damn = Damn It (Non-literal Meaning)

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:59.630
I see you're using that in the literal sense...

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.720
"Go to Hell!"

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:04.890
God Damn = Damn It (Non-literal Meaning)
Literal Meaning: God Will Condemn you to Hell!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.550
After all, doing that is the core aspect of her job.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:09.430
Well, it wouldn't be an overstatement
to say female cats hunting their prey

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.270
have the most merciless dispositions
in the entire animal kingdom.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:16.230
Now, when you have one this massive in size...

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:19.990
Ah, she's fallen asleep!

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.950
Kasha has gone to sleep!

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.280
What's the deal with that?!

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:27.780
Well, it's simply a case of living according
to her instincts, isn't it?!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:30.500
Now that's a cat... a cat in its truest form.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:33.670
I waited around forever for the match to start...

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.960
I was tired as soon as I got out here.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.040
Let me sleep for a bit.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:43.340
M-Miss! Come on!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.050
I thought she'd be raring to go, but she's proved fickle.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:48.220
Talk about playing by "cat rules"!

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.890
Mustard's unable to challenge the sleeping cat to a fight!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.140
Annoying... how annoying...

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:55.480
The cat's completely given up on the fight!

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:56.020
You're annoying.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:21:00.530
Here in Hell, we are always recruiting cats
who are willing to fight.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.080
I was completely crushed by Kasha this time around.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:14.250
I trained at the temple the other day,
but it seems it wasn't enough.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.580
I need to train harder and harder.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:22.510
As of right now, there's no question
that Kasha is far stronger mentally than I am.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:27.760
I'll make sure I don't lose the mental battle next time.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.350
Please do your best.

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:31.970
Hup!

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:32.770
Your defenses are weak!

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.230
Attack without mercy!

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.270
Hi-yah!

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:45.320
What's the deal with that guy
who's facing off against Miss Mustard, meow?

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:49.660
That's human business.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:51.280
Hi-yah!

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:52.580
That's the way!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:10.760
Uso yo. Janakya naze koko ni tadoritsuku no?
That's a lie. If not, why do you find your way here?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:17.350
Enma-sama no mae de nao shira o kiru no ne
Even in front of Lord Enma, you feign ignorance

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:23.280
Baka ne. Dakedo sonna toko tamaranakute
You're an idiot. But I can't get enough of that aspect of you

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:29.660
Teitaraku. Onaji tsumi kasanetsuzuketa
What a predicament. You continued to repeat the same sin

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:34.950
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:36.330
(E?)
(Huh?)
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:41.170
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
(Dogii!)
(Startling!)

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:49.130
Tensei o matazu shounetsu no mama ni
Without waiting for reincarnation, while still in the scorching heat

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:55.180
Asa hiru eien ai o kushizashi narabete
Morning, midday, and eternally skewer desires and line them up

00:22:55.430 --> 00:22:58.350
Gutsu gutsu mou! Nie nie da yo
Already simmering! It's boiling

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.770
Yuuge wa jigoku de hot pot
Supper is a hot pot in Hell

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:07.990
Nita mono doushi ni oniai no oshioki
For people who are alike, a suitable punishment

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:11.110
Juu juu achi! Koge koge da yo
Sizzling hot! It's burned to a crisp

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:14.410
Anata to jigoku de hotcake
Hotcakes with you in Hell

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:19.830
Tokoyo no suna ni naru made
Until they become forever-unchanging sand

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.800
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:29.630
Long, long ago, down by the Sanzu River
there was an old man and woman.

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:29.220
AND

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:30.840
Then the old man went to the mountains?

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:30.720
BUT

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:33.260
He went to the Offices of Enma
to beg to get Maki's autograph.

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:33.760
SO

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:33.760
Huh?!

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:36.560
Maki will be hosting a cooking segment
on a new TV show together with Miki.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:39.730
WE PRESENT:
THE STRIPPING HAG
AND CLOTHES-HANGING GEEZER
AND

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.730
CHEF MIKI
PLEASE ENJOY!

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:37.930
Where'd the old woman go?!

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:39.140
She's at the river.
